---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Same melody, different mode — why a scale's shape changes its mood">
  <header>
    <nav aria-label="Primary">
      <a href="./">Home</a>
    </nav>
  </header>
  <main>
    <h1>The same nine notes, four different moods</h1>
    <p data-testid="intro">
      This is the same short melody — <strong>1‑2‑3‑4‑5‑6‑5‑3‑1</strong>, stated
      as scale degrees, not pitches — played through four different musical
      modes. Nothing about the tune changes. What changes is which 7 notes
      each mode picks out, and that alone is enough to make it sound bright,
      sad, bittersweet or tense. Click a mode to hear it, and watch the ring
      light up.
    </p>

    <section aria-labelledby="wheel-heading">
      <h2 id="wheel-heading">Play a mode</h2>
      <div class="mode-buttons" role="group" aria-label="Mode">
        <button type="button" data-mode-button="ionian" aria-pressed="true">Ionian (major)</button>
        <button type="button" data-mode-button="aeolian" aria-pressed="false">Aeolian (minor)</button>
        <button type="button" data-mode-button="dorian" aria-pressed="false">Dorian</button>
        <button type="button" data-mode-button="phrygian" aria-pressed="false">Phrygian</button>
      </div>

      <div id="mode-label" class="mode-label" data-testid="mode-label"></div>
      <div id="wheel" class="wheel" data-testid="wheel"></div>
      <p class="hint">
        The 7 big circles are the piano's white keys (naturals); the 5 small
        ones nested between them are the black keys (accidentals) — a fixed
        layout, the same for every mode. Whichever 7 notes light up in color
        are this mode's scale, chosen from among those 12; the one with a
        dark outline is the note currently sounding.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <script src="../scripts/main.ts"></script>
</Layout>
